    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0562" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg492"/>

                <head>No. 283.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 18,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 15th instant in relation to the action which Her Majesty’s
                    Government has taken with reference to the decree of the Venezuelan Government
                        <pb facs="0563" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/> requiring ships’ papers to be
                    deposited with the port officers, and to inform you that the American minister
                    at Caracas has been advised that Her Majesty’s minister at that capital will act
                    in concert with him in the matter.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
